; 27-tokenize.kurt

; `tokenize` is a peek under the hood: it shows how a piece of source text is
; split into tokens, before any parsing happens.  Handy when something
; doesn't parse the way you expect, and you want to check whether Kurt even
; split it into the symbols you thought it would.

; the trailing `$$$` in the output below is just Kurt's internal end-of-input marker,
; always appended -- harmless, not part of your actual source text.
bool A, B
tokenize A implies B      ; [A, implies, B]  $$$
